who reads, to do what, and how they read build the structure: the
nodes, and their order.

  purpose          mode             structure
  decide to adopt  skim, once       what it is, what it promises, limits
  get started      follow, doing    steps in run order, one working result
  do a task        scan for a goal  one node per task, named by the goal
  look up a thing  jump in, out     one node per thing, signature first
  understand why   read slowly      the model first, then the cases
  call a module    scan             public surface, what it promises
  change a module  read, trace      core first, then internals
  review a module  read once        top down, each step one level
  debug a module   follow a run     entrypoint down, in execution order

the medium sets the unit, the structure fills it — `general/medium`.
a module's order: `programming/moduleorder`, `programming/methodorder`.

name purpose and mode in a line at the top; a wrong guess then costs one
line. where nothing names them: `general/outline`.

the test: name the purpose, then a question its reader arrives with. the
answer sits in one node. in two, the cut serves another purpose — a cut
by when, once and always, splits whatever has both. a node serving two
purposes, a quickstart that stops to explain why, is two documents.
